ail those headshots there  are a variety of class skills that  reward precision kills and every bit of  extra damage buys you a little more  space between the masses and yourself  use your double or triple jump to eject  from any situation that grows too hairy  and try not to get cornered or it's not  going to be pretty the class differences  aren't as pronounced below the beta  level cap of 8 but at higher level play  the hunter has the potential to take on  a heavier stealth and melee focus than  any other guardian the Blade Dancer  subclass becomes available at level 15  and unlocks the cloaking ability  encourages backstabbing and sneaking for  massive damage and charges the hunters  blade with arc light for devastating  melee strikes and special abilities  such as an area of effect blast there's  also a blink that replaces your double  jump allowing blade dancing hunters to  teleport into battle and execute a blink  strike for some bonus damage regardless  of level and subclass the hunter  strategy comes down to mobility and  momentum staying mobile will keep you  alive long enough to gain momentum and  momentum will allow you to do the Lord's  work my son killing aliens skills like  gunslingers trance caused back-to-back  headshots to increase weapons stability  while chain of woe decreases reload  speed in the exact same way other skills  also extend art blade duration during  melee killing sprees and regenerate  health with blink strikes thus while  taking care is essential to the hunter  survival once you get the ball rolling  be sure to keep that murder train on the  tracks play your cards right and the  Fallen won't even see you coming  you
 

